  "declared_proposition": "Let n_i be an aperiodic accelerated odd Collatz orbit and suppose n_i is at least its odd start n for 0<=i<h. With S_h the sum of the first h valuations, its affine correction C_h satisfies C_h <= (3 ln 2)^(-1) sum_(j<h) 1/(n+2j) <= H(n,h), where H(n,h)=(3 ln 2)^(-1)[1/n+(1/2)ln(1+2(h-1)/n)]. Therefore any aperiodic orbit that never descends must obey S_h-h log2(3)<=H(n,h)=O(log h) at every prefix.",
  "mathematical_argument": "Aperiodicity makes the n_i distinct. Since they are odd and at least n, their increasing rearrangement dominates n,n+2,... . Use log2(1+x)<=x/ln 2 and then the decreasing-function integral bound for sum 1/(n+2j). The exact identity log2(n_h/n)=h log2(3)-S_h+C_h shows that excess above H forces descent.",
